And I'm not talking about with MAME emulation or anything.

00:32:34.100 --> 00:32:42.700
It's just been released on many arcade collections from Atari so that you can play the actual Gauntlet to Arcade now with four players and everything.

00:32:42.820 --> 00:32:46.060
Does that diminish at all this NES entry?

00:32:47.780 --> 00:32:49.900
In 2025, sure.

00:32:51.020 --> 00:32:52.240
Right. Yeah, of course.

00:32:52.380 --> 00:32:54.520
Nobody cares about that in 1990.

00:32:54.880 --> 00:33:00.820
But you have to consider that with a lot of these games that get ported to the arcade,

00:33:00.820 --> 00:33:04.880
we always talk about, well, was the arcade version the best version?

