00:35:26.720 --> 00:35:30.120
Huh. I didn't confirm that, so I'm just spreading misinformation.

00:35:30.440 --> 00:35:32.240
You read that on the Wikipedia page?

00:35:32.400 --> 00:35:33.340
I don't mind it.

00:35:33.400 --> 00:35:35.760
Yeah, that's where you go for misinformation these days.

00:35:37.320 --> 00:35:43.160
And then while we're here doing what essentially is like miscellaneous information, this isn't

00:35:43.160 --> 00:35:45.720
anything about Gauntlet 2, but it's about Gauntlet.

00:35:46.180 --> 00:35:51.140
The next game in this series, Gauntlet the Third Encounter, which is not a good name.

00:35:52.540 --> 00:35:56.800
Right? Gauntlet the Third.

00:35:56.800 --> 00:35:59.120
Gauntlet the Third Encounter.

00:36:01.540 --> 00:36:02.740
Gauntlet squared.

00:36:03.280 --> 00:36:04.680
No, sorry. Gauntlet cubed.

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:09.680
Gaunt 3T. Were they going for like Close Encounters of the Third Kind vibe?

00:36:10.020 --> 00:36:12.020
Like, were they trying to play off that?

00:36:12.220 --> 00:36:13.680
I think it's...

00:36:13.680 --> 00:36:15.500
I think it's fine.

00:36:15.800 --> 00:36:19.600
I don't think it's as ridiculous as...

00:36:19.600 --> 00:36:23.960
You know, now you get sequels and it's always like...

00:36:25.040 --> 00:36:29.360
Like... IP2 Reckoning.

00:36:30.220 --> 00:36:32.560
IP2 Reawakening. Oh no, I think we're done with subtitles.

00:36:32.760 --> 00:36:34.020
I feel like we're done with subtitles.

00:36:34.160 --> 00:36:35.880
I think you just get IP number 2.

00:36:36.480 --> 00:36:37.340
Yeah, but...

00:36:37.340 --> 00:36:38.440
Right? I guess the last...

00:36:38.440 --> 00:36:41.100
We're about to get Nintendo Switch 2.

00:36:41.180 --> 00:36:42.840
They're not even going to call it Super Switch.

00:36:42.940 --> 00:36:47.220
This is bullshit. And yeah, they've just been naming sequels like the name of the original games.

00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:50.880
And now they're just like pretending that these games didn't exist before.

00:36:51.060 --> 00:36:52.060
So, you know what?

00:36:52.060 --> 00:36:53.680
I'm fine with Gauntlet the Third.

00:36:54.320 --> 00:36:55.720
Okay. The Third Encounter.

00:36:55.900 --> 00:36:57.020
Just make sure you get the whole thing in there.

00:36:57.080 --> 00:36:58.840
No, no, no. It's like...

00:36:58.840 --> 00:37:00.760
What was that? Disney Channel?

00:37:01.840 --> 00:37:02.700
Beethoven the Third?

00:37:05.740 --> 00:37:07.480
The dog? The dog.

00:37:09.080 --> 00:37:10.040
Beethoven the dog?

00:37:10.220 --> 00:37:12.680
I think it was like Beethoven the Third.

00:37:14.560 --> 00:37:15.740
Beethoven the Third.

00:37:15.940 --> 00:37:18.760
Okay, sure. I didn't know he was the third.

00:37:18.900 --> 00:37:20.280
Who's the second? Oh, it's Beethoven's...

00:37:20.280 --> 00:37:22.900
It's Beethoven's Third.

00:37:23.680 --> 00:37:24.580
Okay, okay.

00:37:25.200 --> 00:37:26.740
Is that in reference to a symphony?

00:37:27.020 --> 00:37:28.380
It is in reference to a symphony.

00:37:28.560 --> 00:37:30.600
But I prefer Beethoven the Third.

00:37:32.220 --> 00:37:35.980
Everybody finds a clever way to work in a reference for their third.

00:37:36.080 --> 00:37:38.220
They could have tried Beethoven's The Third Encounter.

00:37:38.440 --> 00:37:39.260
That's true.

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:42.480
Close Encounters of the Beethoven kind.

00:37:42.680 --> 00:37:44.560
Hey, it's a dog.

00:37:45.200 --> 00:37:51.760
Anyway, Gauntlet the Third Encounter, the reason I brought it up at all, is because it uses the box art from Gauntlet 1 on the NES.

00:37:52.760 --> 00:37:56.820
That's weird. I've never heard of that happening for another video game.

00:37:56.980 --> 00:37:59.140
They couldn't hire somebody to just draw something else?

00:37:59.140 --> 00:38:02.340
They were not accepting commissions for a new box art.

00:38:02.540 --> 00:38:04.920
They were like, we have to use one that already exists.

00:38:05.060 --> 00:38:08.140
And keep in mind, Gauntlet the Third Encounter, we will not play it.

00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:09.780
It will not come out on the NES.

00:38:10.000 --> 00:38:13.420
So they're just saying, well, nobody will notice because these kids don't own an NES.

00:38:13.560 --> 00:38:15.120
They own whatever this system is.

00:38:15.720 --> 00:38:20.260
It's the same manual. What a weird cost-cutting measure.

00:38:20.860 --> 00:38:23.920
Yeah. I mean, did they send a manual with the game at least?

00:38:23.940 --> 00:38:26.080
Or did they just give you the manual from the first game?

00:38:26.440 --> 00:38:34.440
Yeah. Well, I've talked about just about everything I wanted to talk about.

00:38:34.700 --> 00:38:40.520
So I think we got to talk about the last thing we have to talk about, which of course is the Essential Games list.

00:38:44.180 --> 00:38:47.540
Gauntlet 2 is great pick-up-and-play fun.

00:38:47.840 --> 00:38:53.360
And it's the kind of game that you really don't need to know anything about to jump right into,

00:38:53.520 --> 00:38:56.300
which is why I'm kind of disappointed that nobody played this game with me.

00:38:56.540 --> 00:38:58.540
I'm not throwing any shade at any specific person.

00:38:58.540 --> 00:39:00.920
But you could have played this game because it's very easy to play.

00:39:01.080 --> 00:39:03.520
It's very accessible. You don't die right away either.

00:39:03.880 --> 00:39:07.000
It is a challenging game as the game goes on.

00:39:07.160 --> 00:39:09.740
I'm not saying you'll live forever or see the end.

00:39:09.800 --> 00:39:11.000
No. Far from it.

00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:15.780
But you will enjoy the moment-to-moment gameplay while you are holding the controller.

00:39:15.920 --> 00:39:17.180
And I really do believe that.

00:39:17.320 --> 00:39:24.320
I agree with Sean that if you can play this with four people, especially two or three drinks in,

00:39:24.460 --> 00:39:26.080
I bet you're going to have an even better time.

00:39:26.080 --> 00:39:31.460
This is not the kind of game that I felt like I needed to make any forward progress in.

00:39:31.660 --> 00:39:36.320
I didn't feel like I needed to, because there isn't the story, I didn't feel like I needed to get to a certain point.

00:39:36.540 --> 00:39:38.600
Just like I do with most shmups.

00:39:38.660 --> 00:39:43.100
I don't feel disappointed when I die in a shmup and now it's back to the beginning.

00:39:43.260 --> 00:39:46.020
It's like, no, the actual gameplay was fun.

00:39:46.020 --> 00:39:56.200
And I think that's something, not to throw shade at Dragon Warrior 2, but that's a problem with some of these older games that we now have more modern advancements for.

00:39:56.400 --> 00:40:05.500
It's like, Gauntlet 2 doesn't necessarily need any new modern features added to it to be the game that it was in 1990.

00:40:05.500 --> 00:40:11.180
Whereas like Dragon Warrior 2, we could think of countless improvements that the JRPG genre has had.

00:40:11.940 --> 00:40:17.320
All that to say, though, Gauntlet 2 is far from a perfect game here.

00:40:17.580 --> 00:40:20.820
And while it is fun, it is party fun.

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:23.280
It is not one of the great video games.

00:40:23.280 --> 00:40:30.680
I actually feel like the actual game itself is fun just because it's kind of mindless and you're just doing whatever you want to do.

00:40:30.720 --> 00:40:36.780
But you're not necessarily getting, you know, an unforgettable video game experience.

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:38.380
Now, could you have that with four players?

00:40:38.740 --> 00:40:41.560
Sure. But I think that's because of your friends, not because of the game.

00:40:41.720 --> 00:40:44.880
So I am not putting it on the essential games list and that might sound cheap.

00:40:45.140 --> 00:40:51.580
But if you don't like that, you can just go to Electronic Gaming Monthly and they'll consider it the third best game of all time.

00:40:51.880 --> 00:40:55.040
Sean? Yeah, I agree.

00:40:55.360 --> 00:40:59.220
I think that like I was saying and I kind of got ahead of myself there.

00:40:59.420 --> 00:41:01.120
This is a game I would own.

00:41:02.340 --> 00:41:07.360
But I would sort of a game I probably talked about before.

00:41:08.800 --> 00:41:12.240
The more modern example is like War of the Monsters.

00:41:12.520 --> 00:41:22.040
Like that is a game that I think is really cool on PS2 that you're just a kaiju and you fight other kaiju and you blow up buildings.

00:41:22.040 --> 00:41:24.400
And it's like just a big playground.

00:41:25.580 --> 00:41:29.660
But I just, I really like that game just for those things.

00:41:29.660 --> 00:41:47.540
I think those things make it like a 10 out of 10 game in the same way that Iris really like how immediate everything is in this game and how you feel like you're making progress even though there's really no need to make that kind of progress.

00:41:48.720 --> 00:41:50.820
But it's just fun in that instance.

00:41:50.820 --> 00:41:59.740
And yeah, I'd imagine that it's a lot more fun with other people getting in each other's way, especially those levels that warn you that there's friendly fire.

00:41:59.740 --> 00:42:01.740
I feel like that's something we missed out on.

00:42:03.140 --> 00:42:07.280
But yeah, I also can't say that those things make it an essential game.

00:42:07.760 --> 00:42:10.080
But yeah, definitely a good one.

00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:16.760
So without going through the entire Gauntlet catalog here.

00:42:17.820 --> 00:42:20.320
No, I meant like Gauntlet as a franchise.

00:42:21.280 --> 00:42:29.900
Without going through it all, like would you play any like of the ones that play closer to this arcade experience?

00:42:29.900 --> 00:42:32.840
Or would you look to play even further than that?

00:42:32.920 --> 00:42:35.660
Ones that kind of tried to take the IP beyond it?

00:42:35.880 --> 00:42:37.180
Where do you stand on Gauntlet?

00:42:37.180 --> 00:42:41.580
I think that even the more modern ones, I think those are still pretty much arcade games.

00:42:41.660 --> 00:42:49.720
I could be wrong, but at least the one that I played, whether that was the PlayStation 1 or the PlayStation 2 one, it was pretty arcade-y.

00:42:49.880 --> 00:42:54.420
So I don't think it really ever went too far from its roots, but I could be wrong.

00:42:55.020 --> 00:42:58.040
So will you be checking out another Gauntlet game?

00:42:58.320 --> 00:43:04.340
Yeah. And would it be Gauntlet the Third Encounter or Gauntlet 3, the Final Quest?

00:43:04.560 --> 00:43:06.100
It would be Gauntlet the Third.

00:43:07.180 --> 00:43:12.100
You can't call a game Gauntlet 3 after you already called a game Gauntlet the Third.

00:43:14.360 --> 00:43:18.020
Do you know why they called it Gauntlet 3 though?

00:43:18.220 --> 00:43:23.920
I thought maybe that they were just like two different games made by two different teams with the same IP.

00:43:23.920 --> 00:43:24.920
It's not that?

00:43:25.360 --> 00:43:27.080
No, it's pretty much exactly that.

00:43:27.560 --> 00:43:32.360
Gauntlet 3 was released on like actual stuff.

00:43:32.360 --> 00:43:37.980
And Gauntlet the Third was released on the Atari Lynx.

00:43:38.280 --> 00:43:39.300
Ah, okay.

00:43:39.460 --> 00:43:43.640
So I think it was like, oh, we need a big, you know, the Atari Lynx.

00:43:43.780 --> 00:43:47.920
Obviously, Atari is the owner of the Gauntlet franchise.

00:43:47.920 --> 00:43:50.460
They were like, oh, let's get a Gauntlet game on here.

00:43:50.580 --> 00:43:51.560
Let's make a big deal about it.

00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:56.460
And then nobody bought a Lynx because it took like six batteries or something to get up and running.

00:43:57.040 --> 00:44:00.440
So instead we got like, let's try that again.

00:44:00.640 --> 00:44:03.000
And they did Gauntlet 3, the Final Quest.

00:44:03.200 --> 00:44:07.140
And whenever there's a Final Quest, of course, you'll get Gauntlet 4 sooner or later.

00:44:07.580 --> 00:44:08.600
How much sooner?

00:44:08.840 --> 00:44:12.340
Very soon. Gauntlet 4 came out.

00:44:12.340 --> 00:44:13.360
What?

00:44:13.540 --> 00:44:16.720
Let's see. Two years after the Final Quest?

00:44:16.980 --> 00:44:18.500
Well, it's a reboot, you know?

00:44:19.420 --> 00:44:20.440
Yeah, that's true.

00:44:20.500 --> 00:44:21.620
They stopped doing subtitles.

00:44:21.900 --> 00:44:23.100
So it's just like modern games.

00:44:23.240 --> 00:44:25.680
Gauntlet. Endgame.

00:44:27.040 --> 00:44:42.920
End episode. Endgame.
